# User email format

## Intent

A stored user email is a real address: local part, domain, and a letter TLD of at least 2 characters. `jgi@ghi.com` is valid. `user@localhost`, `a@b.c`, blanks, and `a..b@x.com` are not.

## Do not regress

1. Create, update, register, and platform-staff create call `EmailAddressRules.require` after trim/lowercase. Do not persist `UserLoginUtil.normalizeEmail` alone.
2. DTO email fields use `@Pattern(regexp = EmailAddressRules.PATTERN)`. Do not rely on Jakarta `@Email` — it treats `""` as valid and allows a domain without a TLD.
3. Login lookup stays normalize-only. A bad login email is a failed login, not a validation error.
